# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# JetBrains IDE configuration
.idea

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
/vendor/

# Dev files
/bin/*
# Anchored. Unanchored, this matched any path segment named `coverage`
# anywhere in the tree, so the `core/coverage` package was ignored and would
# have been committed as nothing at all. The artifacts `make coverage`
# actually writes are coverage.out (covered by *.out above) and coverage.html.
/coverage
/coverage.html

# Docker volumes and data
/.docker/
.env
docker-compose.override.yaml
integration/reports
test-reports
integration-test

# A leaked SQLite dev database. `--dev-url "sqlite://dev?mode=memory"` opens a
# RELATIVE FILE named `dev` rather than an in-memory database, so a test that
# passes that spelling writes one into the package directory it runs in. Tracked
# as stokaro/ptah#1819; ignored here so it cannot be committed again while the
# underlying behavior is being fixed.
cmd/atlas/dev

# Ptah Assist writes each conversation here, in the project it was about. The
# file holds the conversation and whatever Ptah read on the model's behalf, so
# it is somebody's local working state rather than something to commit --
# `ptah assist --ephemeral` keeps no record at all (stokaro/ptah#1489).
.ptah/sessions/

# goreleaser writes its build output here. `docs/release_process.md` asks for a
# local snapshot before every release, and that snapshot is 1.2 GB.
/dist/
